---
/**
 * VerificationSurfaces — the three example products, drawn by what you can
 * actually observe in each: a screen, a screen plus an evidence trail, and
 * no screen at all.
 *
 * The point of the picture is the third card: a strategy built around clicking
 * has nothing to say about Polaris.
 */
---

<figure class="lu-figure surfaces">
  <div class="lu-figure__frame">
    <ul class="cards">
      <li class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 160 96" role="img" aria-label="A browser window with a pointer clicking a button">
          <rect class="pane" x="24" y="12" width="112" height="72" rx="6" />
          <line class="hair" x1="24" y1="28" x2="136" y2="28" />
          <circle class="dot" cx="33" cy="20" r="2" />
          <circle class="dot" cx="41" cy="20" r="2" />
          <rect class="row" x="34" y="38" width="58" height="5" rx="2.5" />
          <rect class="row" x="34" y="50" width="40" height="5" rx="2.5" />
          <rect class="cta" x="34" y="64" width="36" height="12" rx="4" />
          <path class="pointer" d="M92 60 l0 16 l4.5 -4.5 l3 6.5 l3 -1.5 l-3 -6.5 l6 0 z" />
        </svg>
        <h3>Trailhead Outfitters</h3>
        <p>A screen, and money behind it. You can watch a person do the thing.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 160 96" role="img" aria-label="A browser window with a keyboard focus ring, beside a stack of evidence documents">
          <rect class="pane" x="10" y="12" width="92" height="72" rx="6" />
          <line class="hair" x1="10" y1="28" x2="102" y2="28" />
          <circle class="dot" cx="19" cy="20" r="2" />
          <circle class="dot" cx="27" cy="20" r="2" />
          <rect class="row" x="20" y="38" width="48" height="5" rx="2.5" />
          <rect class="focus" x="16" y="50" width="58" height="18" rx="4" />
          <rect class="row" x="20" y="56" width="34" height="5" rx="2.5" />
          <g class="docs">
            <rect class="doc" x="116" y="26" width="32" height="42" rx="3" />
            <rect class="doc doc--front" x="110" y="34" width="32" height="42" rx="3" />
            <line class="doc-line" x1="116" y1="44" x2="136" y2="44" />
            <line class="doc-line" x1="116" y1="52" x2="132" y2="52" />
            <line class="doc-line" x1="116" y1="60" x2="136" y2="60" />
          </g>
        </svg>
        <h3>Beechwood Health</h3>
        <p>A screen you must reach by keyboard, and a trail somebody signs.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 160 96" role="img" aria-label="An empty dashed box with events entering, a carrier call leaving, and a webhook returning">
          <rect class="pane pane--empty" x="46" y="26" width="68" height="44" rx="6" />
          <text class="pane-label" x="80" y="52">no screen</text>
          <path class="flow" d="M8 40 L44 40" marker-end="url(#vs-arrow)" />
          <text class="flow-label" x="8" y="32">order</text>
          <path class="flow" d="M116 40 L152 40" marker-end="url(#vs-arrow)" />
          <text class="flow-label flow-label--end" x="152" y="32">carrier</text>
          <path class="flow flow--back" d="M148 58 L116 58" marker-end="url(#vs-arrow-dim)" />
          <text class="flow-label flow-label--end" x="152" y="76">webhook, twice</text>
          <defs>
            <marker id="vs-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="arrowhead" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
            </marker>
            <marker id="vs-arrow-dim" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="arrowhead arrowhead--dim" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
            </marker>
          </defs>
        </svg>
        <h3>Polaris Freight</h3>
        <p>Nothing to click. Events in, carriers out, and answers that come back late.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="lu-figure__caption">
    Three products, three different things you are allowed to observe. A strategy
    that only works on the first card is not a strategy.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.875rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--lu-radius-control);
    background: var(--lu-surface-2);
  }

  .card svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 590;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .pane {
    fill: var(--lu-surface-1);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .pane--empty {
    fill: none;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
  }

  .pane-label {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 9px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .hair {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .dot {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .row {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .cta {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .pointer {
    fill: var(--lu-marker);
  }

  .focus {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--lu-marker);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }

  .doc {
    fill: var(--lu-surface-1);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .doc-line {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }

  .flow {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .flow--back {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }

  .arrowhead {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .arrowhead--dim {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .flow-label {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 8px;
  }

  .flow-label--end {
    text-anchor: end;
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .card svg {
      max-width: 260px;
    }
  }
</style>
